{{!
    @template theme_erasight/landing

    The priced course grid + testimonials + team-pricing band inserted below
    the hero on the front page (see layout/frontpage.php, templates/frontpage.mustache).
    New, theme-owned markup — not a core override, and deliberately its own
    small card markup here rather than reusing core_course/coursecard.mustache,
    since that shared template also renders on the dashboard/catalog where a
    price shouldn't appear for an already-enrolled student.

    Context: courses (array of id/fullname/category/shortdescription/
    courseimage/detailurl/price, where price is itself an object with a
    "formatted" string, or absent; category and shortdescription are both
    optional — a course with no category or a blank summary just omits
    that line) plus a separate hascourses boolean, populartitle/viewalllabel/viewallurl,
    feedbacktitle, testimonials (array of quote/name/role/initials) plus a
    separate hastestimonials boolean, teamstitle/teamsbody/teamscta/teamsctaurl.

    Also: valueprops (array of title/body) plus a separate hasvalueprops
    boolean; audienceindividualstitle/audienceindividualsbody/
    audienceteamstitle/audienceteamsbody (a static two-column block, not an
    array, so no guard boolean needed); scenariostitle, scenarios (array of
    problem/outcome) plus a separate hasscenarios boolean; and
    closingctatitle/closingctaprimarylabel/closingctaprimaryurl/
    closingctasecondarylabel/closingctasecondaryurl.

    The hascourses/hastestimonials/hasvalueprops/hasscenarios booleans exist
    because Mustache sections have only one behavior for an array: repeat
    the block once per element. Wrapping a whole section (heading included)
    directly in a courses or testimonials section tag is not an "if
    non-empty" guard — with 3 testimonials it rendered that entire section,
    heading and all, 3 times on the live site. Only the courses section
    looked fine, coincidentally, because there was exactly 1 course to
    iterate. The outer guard and the inner loop must use different keys,
    never the same tag twice.

    NOTE: deliberately described in prose above, not as a literal JSON
    example — a nested JSON object here previously produced two adjacent
    closing-brace characters, which closed this Mustache comment early
    (it ends at the first such occurrence it scans past, not a matched
    one) and leaked the rest of this comment plus broke the template's
    own section boundaries into the live page. Never write two
    closing-brace characters next to each other anywhere in this
    comment block, quoted or not.
}}
<div class="erasight-landing">
    {{#hasvalueprops}}
    <div class="erasight-landing-section">
        <div class="erasight-valueprops">
            {{#valueprops}}
            <div class="erasight-valueprop">
                <h4>{{title}}</h4>
                <p>{{body}}</p>
            </div>
            {{/valueprops}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/hasvalueprops}}

    {{#hascourses}}
    <div class="erasight-landing-section">
        <div class="erasight-landing-head">
            <h3>{{populartitle}}</h3>
            <a href="{{viewallurl}}">{{viewalllabel}}</a>
        </div>
        <div class="erasight-landing-grid">
            {{#courses}}
            <a class="erasight-landing-card" href="{{detailurl}}">
                <div class="erasight-landing-thumb" style='background-image: url("{{{courseimage}}}");'></div>
                <div class="erasight-landing-cardbody">
                    {{#category}}<div class="erasight-landing-cat">{{category}}</div>{{/category}}
                    <h4>{{fullname}}</h4>
                    {{#shortdescription}}<p class="erasight-landing-desc">{{shortdescription}}</p>{{/shortdescription}}
                    {{#price}}<div class="erasight-landing-price">{{formatted}}</div>{{/price}}
                </div>
            </a>
            {{/courses}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/hascourses}}

    <div class="erasight-landing-section">
        <div class="erasight-audience">
            <div class="erasight-audience-col">
                <h4>{{audienceindividualstitle}}</h4>
                <p>{{audienceindividualsbody}}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="erasight-audience-col">
                <h4>{{audienceteamstitle}}</h4>
                <p>{{audienceteamsbody}}</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {{#hastestimonials}}
    <div class="erasight-landing-section erasight-landing-section-alt">
        <div class="erasight-landing-head"><h3>{{feedbacktitle}}</h3></div>
        <div class="erasight-testimonial-grid">
            {{#testimonials}}
            <div class="erasight-tcard">
                <blockquote>&ldquo;{{quote}}&rdquo;</blockquote>
                <div class="erasight-tcard-who">
                    <div class="erasight-tcard-avatar">{{initials}}</div>
                    <div><strong>{{name}}</strong><span>{{role}}</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>
            {{/testimonials}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/hastestimonials}}

    {{#hasscenarios}}
    <div class="erasight-landing-section erasight-landing-section-alt">
        <div class="erasight-landing-head"><h3>{{scenariostitle}}</h3></div>
        <div class="erasight-scenario-grid">
            {{#scenarios}}
            <div class="erasight-scenario-card">
                <div class="erasight-scenario-problem">{{problem}}</div>
                <div class="erasight-scenario-outcome">{{outcome}}</div>
            </div>
            {{/scenarios}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/hasscenarios}}

    <div class="erasight-landing-section">
        <div class="erasight-teams-band">
            <div>
                <h3>{{teamstitle}}</h3>
                <p>{{teamsbody}}</p>
                <a class="erasight-hero-btn erasight-hero-btn-primary" href="{{teamsctaurl}}">{{teamscta}}</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="erasight-landing-section erasight-closing-cta">
        <h3>{{closingctatitle}}</h3>
        <div class="erasight-hero-cta">
            <a class="erasight-hero-btn erasight-hero-btn-primary" href="{{closingctaprimaryurl}}">{{closingctaprimarylabel}}</a>
            <a class="erasight-hero-btn erasight-hero-btn-secondary-alt" href="{{closingctasecondaryurl}}">{{closingctasecondarylabel}}</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
